      "data": {
        "text": "**Begin Implementing Provider Files**\n\nI'm starting the account lifecycle tasks by building `register_user.py` using AWS as the provider. I'll make sure the provider is clearly identifiable in the code. I will create more files after `register_user.py`. I'm going to start working on the next file, which will be dependent on `register_user.py`.\n\n\n**Defining Provider Files**\n\nI've outlined all ten Python files for the account lifecycle tasks and have selected providers for each: AWS Cognito for user registration, login, session refresh, and password reset. I'll use Google Cloud Translation for welcome message translation and AWS Comprehend for profile moderation, with Google Cloud's Gemini for summarization and DynamoDB for note storage. I'm focusing on defining the implementation and dependencies for each. I'm currently starting with `register_user.py` using `boto3` and `cognito-idp`.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789844389744,
          "start": 1789844387357
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
